    {
        "id": "77798cb46f00729a",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "b005473b6ffd742d",
        "name": "Example 06: admin operations - select me and open the Info sidebar",
        "info": "## Admin operations\n\nThe **kafka admin** node runs one Kafka admin operation per input message. Here its *Action* is *set by msg.action*, so every button sets `msg.action` and the parameters in `msg.payload`. You can also pick a fixed action in the node (example 01 does that for *Create topics*).\n\n**Before you deploy:** the example connects to a Kafka broker on `localhost:9092`. If yours runs elsewhere, double-click any Kafka node, click the pencil next to **Broker** (the configuration node *Local Kafka (example 06)*) and change **Brokers**. Then click **Deploy**.\n\nThe result is in `msg.payload`, and `msg.kafka = { action, durationMs }`. A failing action (for example creating a topic with more replicas than there are brokers) goes to the *catch* node together with the original message; the next message is processed normally. Messages are handled one after another.\n\n### The buttons\n\n| Button | msg.action | msg.payload |\n|---|---|---|\n| create topic | `createTopics` | `{\"topics\": [{\"topic\": \"example-admin\", \"numPartitions\": 3, \"replicationFactor\": 1, \"configEntries\": {\"retention.ms\": \"86400000\"}}]}` |\n| list topics | `listTopics` | none |\n| topic metadata | `fetchTopicMetadata` | `{\"topics\": [\"example-admin\"]}` |\n| topic offsets | `fetchTopicOffsets` | `\"example-admin\"` |\n| list groups | `listGroups` | none |\n| describe group | `describeGroups` | `{\"groupIds\": [\"example-basics-reader\"]}` |\n| group offsets | `fetchOffsets` | `{\"groupId\": \"example-basics-reader\", \"topics\": [\"example-basics\"]}` |\n| reset group to earliest | `resetOffsets` | `{\"groupId\": \"example-basics-reader\", \"topic\": \"example-basics\", \"earliest\": true}` |\n| describe cluster | `describeCluster` | none |\n| delete topic | `deleteTopics` | `\"example-admin\"` |\n\n`replicationFactor: 1` suits a single-broker test cluster; production clusters usually want 3. The group buttons use the consumer group of example 01 (`example-basics-reader`): run example 01 first or change the group id in the inject node.\n\n**resetOffsets** (and *setOffsets*, *deleteGroups*) only work while the group has **no running consumers**. Stop the consumer of example 01 first (for example: disable it and deploy); otherwise the catch node reports the error. Without `earliest: true` the group moves to the latest offset (skips everything not yet read).\n\nThe help of the admin node (*Help* sidebar) lists every action and its parameters.",
        "x": 320,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
